# Test: the configuration netlab renders for a ze node runs, authenticates, and
# answers the show command netlab validation parses.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-netlab-integration AC-9 and AC-10.
#            AC-9  -- `ze config validate` accepts contrib/netlab/golden/r3.conf,
#                     the committed render of contrib/netlab/ze/ze.j2.
#            AC-10 -- a daemon started from that render lets the user the render
#                     declared log in over SSH, and
#                     `ze cli -c "show bgp peer list | json compact"` -- the exact
#                     string contrib/netlab/ze.yml puts in netlab_show_command --
#                     returns output a JSON parser accepts.
# PREVENTS:  two failures that look nothing alike and have the same cause, a
#            contributed artifact nothing executes.
#            1. The templates emit config the parser accepts and the daemon
#               refuses, or refuses to run with. `./le netlab render-check`
#               catches a drifted RENDER; only a daemon catches a drifted
#               RUNTIME, and that check needs netlab installed while this test
#               needs nothing.
#            2. `netlab validate` gets YAML where it asked for JSON. That was
#               real: `ze cli -c "show x | json compact"` ran the pipe and then
#               printFormatted re-rendered its JSON back to YAML under the
#               default --format yaml (internal/component/cli/client/main.go).
#               The user's explicit pipe lost to a flag default, and every
#               netlab validation over a ze node would have failed to parse.
#
# The config under test is the COMMITTED GOLDEN, read through ZE_REPO_ROOT, and
# not a copy pasted into this file. A copy is a second source of truth that goes
# stale the first time the template changes, which is the whole failure this test
# exists to catch. r3 is the node to use: it is the topology's bgp-only node, so
# it carries no OSPF, IS-IS or BFD block, and those need real interfaces that no
# unprivileged test host has.
#
# Two edits are applied to the golden, and each one is asserted to have changed
# something so a rename in the template cannot make this test quietly stop
# testing:
#   - the link addresses 10.1.0.5 / 10.1.0.6 become 127.0.0.1, because a test
#     host has neither and `ze start` then dies on "can't assign requested
#     address";
#   - the SSH port becomes 0 (ephemeral), because the plugin suite runs tests in
#     parallel and the rendered default 2222 is one port for all of them.
# Nothing else is touched. The session never establishes (both ends are this
# host) and it does not need to: `show bgp peer list` reports a configured peer
# either way, which is what netlab validation reads.
#
# DISCRIMINATOR: revert the format-pipe precedence in
# internal/component/cli/client/main.go renderCommandOutput and seq 1 fails at
# the JSON step, because the output is YAML. Break any ze.j2 branch r3 renders
# and it fails earlier, at `ze config validate` or at daemon start.

# Native process driver validates the golden, starts the daemon, authenticates
# over SSH, and parses the exact netlab JSON command.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/netlab-lab-profile:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
